TI  - Optical properties of biological tissues: a review.
PG  - R37-61
LID - 10.1088/0031-9155/58/11/R37 [doi]
AB  - A review of reported tissue optical properties summarizes the 
      wavelength-dependent behavior of scattering and absorption. Formulae are 
      presented for generating the optical properties of a generic tissue with variable 
      amounts of absorbing chromophores (blood, water, melanin, fat, yellow pigments) 
      and a variable balance between small-scale scatterers and large-scale scatterers 
      in the ultrastructures of cells and tissues.
